## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design privacy-preserving, explainable, multi-tenant scoring systems with model versioning and data residency constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Differential privacy controls and masking in explanations
- Tenant isolation and per-tenant policies
- Model versioning, auditing, and explainability fidelity

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-endpoint sketch for generate
app.post('/cca_score/generate', (req, res) => {
  const {tenant_id, user_id, model_version, features} = req.body;
  // validate policy, fetch model, compute score, apply DP if enabled
  res.json({score, explanation});
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test explainability fidelity under DP constraints?
- What edge cases would trigger rollback or audit alerts?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes understanding of secure multi-tenant design, auditable operations, and basic access control in a beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts

- JWT-based auth with tenant_id boundaries
- Row-Level Security or tenant-scoped data stores
- Immutable/append-only audit log with canonical fields
- Model versioning exposure and validation
- End-to-end test strategy for security and data isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo middleware to verify JWT and enforce tenant boundary
function authorize(req) {
  const token = req.headers['authorization'];
  const payload = verifyJwt(token);
  if (!payload || payload.tenant_id !== req.params.tenant_id) throw new Error('Unauthorized');
  return payload;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate audit logs to detect tampering?
- How would you rotate signing keys without downtime?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of consent-driven data minimization, offline safety, and the relationship between consent lifecycle and CCA score calculation.

## Key Concepts
- Consent tokens gate data exposure
- policy_version controls exposure granularity
- Idempotent, offline-safe compute operations
- Per-user data retention settings

## Code Example
```javascript
async function computeCCA(userIdMasked, consentToken, policyVersion) {
  const consent = await consentStore.validate(consentToken, policyVersion);
  if (!consent?.allowed) {
    throw new Error('Not authorized');
  }
  const score = await calculateScore(userIdMasked, consent);
  return { user_id_masked: userIdMasked, cca_score: score };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Gauges how well a candidate designs feature-level gating in a per-user scoring API, a practical knob for privacy, performance, and experimentation.

## Key Concepts
- Feature gating: filter features at the API boundary.
- Deterministic scoring: gating should not introduce nondeterminism.
- Validation & observability: log gating decisions for audits.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: apply feature gating before scoring
function computeScoreWithGating(allFeatures, allowedFeatures){
  const mask = new Set(allowedFeatures || allFeatures.map(f => f.name));
  const included = allFeatures.filter(f => mask.has(f.name));
  return computeScoreFromFeatures(included);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to validate and handle invalid feature names?
- How would you scale gating across multiple model_versions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a robust ingestion and auditing path for a privacy-preserving cca_score with revocation.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotent ingestion and exactly-once processing
- Versioned, tamper-evident ledger and revocation/delta application
- Streaming pipelines and baseline vs. incremental recomputation
- Cryptographic signing and cross-tenant isolation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example signature verification
function verifyShareSignature(share, publicKey) {
  const { payload, signature } = share;
  // verify using chosen crypto (Ed25519/ECDSA)
  return crypto.verify(publicKey, payload, signature);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test revocation at scale (latency, integrity)?
- How would you enforce per-tenant data isolation in a shared ledger?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design privacy-preserving aggregation across tenants, with robust auditability, key-management, and resilience to compromised aggregators.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-tenant policy enforcement
- Threshold homomorphic encryption and distributed decryption
- Tamper-evident ledger with per-tenant audit trails
- Batch verification and replay protection
- Key management and revocation

